    {
      "id": "L2",
      "question": "Do you fully understand what a tool call is and what a context window holds?",
      "title": "Tools and the context window",
      "paragraph": "A language model on its own can only write text. A {tool} lets it act: it is a function, such as reading a file or running a command, described to the model by its name, its inputs and what it does.[1] To use one, the model writes a {tool call}, a short structured request naming the tool and its inputs, and the program around it runs the tool and returns the result. Everything the model can see on a step, its instructions, the conversation, tool calls and their results, sits in its {context window}.[2] The window has a fixed size, counted in {tokens}; when it is full, older content must be dropped or {summarized} before more can come in.",
      "terms": [
        {
          "term": "tool",
          "definition": "A function the model is allowed to ask for, like read_file or run_command. The model never runs it itself; it only asks, and a program runs it.",
          "part": "B2",
          "sources": [
            1
          ]
        },
        {
          "term": "tool call",
          "definition": "The model's request to use a tool: the tool's name plus its inputs, written in a fixed structure (for example edit_file with path auth.ts) so a program can read it.",
          "part": "B3",
          "sources": [
            1
          ]
        },
        {
          "term": "context window",
          "definition": "Everything the model reads before it writes its next token, as one long text. It holds instructions, messages, tool calls and tool results. What is not in it, the model cannot know.",
          "part": "B1",
          "sources": [
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "term": "summarized",
          "definition": "Replaced by a shorter version written by the model, so the key facts stay while most of the space is freed.",
          "sources": [
            2
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Anthropic docs: Tool use with Claude",
          "kind": "doc",
          "url": "https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/agents-and-tools/tool-use/overview"
